1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,247
Obviously the question of what math actually is,

2
00:00:03,347 --> 00:00:05,828
has been debated for much of history.

3
00:00:05,933 --> 00:00:09,029
And due to Godel's incompleteness theorems,

4
00:00:09,129 --> 00:00:11,185
there is no objective answer.

5
00:00:11,333 --> 00:00:14,341
If we visualize the totality of math as a

6
00:00:14,441 --> 00:00:17,905
set, then its border cannot be clearly defined.

7
00:00:18,066 --> 00:00:20,952
Note that we can either choose to visualize

8
00:00:21,052 --> 00:00:24,494
the totality of math syntactically or semantically.

9
00:00:24,666 --> 00:00:27,600
Syntactically this would be the set of all

10
00:00:27,700 --> 00:00:31,646
true mathematical formulas written in first order logic,

11
00:00:31,800 --> 00:00:36,631
and semantically would be the totality of mathematical structures.

12
00:00:36,731 --> 00:00:41,487
Where mathematical structures can be seen as pre-existing eternal

13
00:00:41,587 --> 00:00:44,252
objects in a platonic world of forms.

